            <p><strong>Advancements in Sustainable Infrastructure</strong></p>
            <p>By Dr. Elena Ramirez<br>
            Department of Civil Engineering, MIT</p>
            <p>The construction industry is at a pivotal moment in its evolution. As global demand for infrastructure continues to outpace supply, engineers are turning to innovative technologies that promise not only greater efficiency but also lower environmental impact. This issue presents a comprehensive overview of the latest breakthroughs in sustainable building practices, with particular focus on the integration of smart materials and digital twins.</p>

            <p>According to recent data from the World Economic Forum, the construction sector accounts for approximately 36% of global carbon emissions. By adopting circular economy principles—recycling, reusing, and reducing waste—engineers can dramatically cut these figures. One promising method involves the use of bio-based composites derived from agricultural waste, which offer comparable strength to traditional concrete while reducing embodied carbon by up to 70%.</p>

